---
import BlockLayout from '../../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import { reviewsBySlug } from '../../data/reviews';

const review = reviewsBySlug.get('the-listening-grove')!;
const title = review.title;
const description = review.dek;
const pointcastUrl = 'https://pointcast.xyz/listening-grove';
const standaloneUrl = review.standaloneUrl;

const reviewJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Review',
  '@id': 'https://pointcast.xyz/reviews/the-listening-grove#review',
  url: 'https://pointcast.xyz/reviews/the-listening-grove',
  name: title,
  headline: title,
  description,
  datePublished: '2026-07-25',
  inLanguage: 'en-US',
  author: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'PointCast Review Lab',
    url: 'https://pointcast.xyz/reviews',
  },
  itemReviewed: {
    '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
    name: 'The Listening Grove',
    url: pointcastUrl,
    applicationCategory: 'MultimediaApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Web',
    softwareVersion: '4',
  },
  reviewRating: {
    '@type': 'Rating',
    ratingValue: 4.5,
    bestRating: 5,
    worstRating: 1,
  },
};
---

<BlockLayout legacy
  title={title}
  description={description}
  image="/images/listening-grove-review/listening-grove-review-og.jpg"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(reviewJsonLd)} />

  <article class="review">
    <div class="review__bar" aria-label="Review information">
      <a href="/" class="review__brand">POINTCAST</a>
      <a href="/reviews">REVIEWS</a>
      <span>JULY 2026</span>
      <a href="/reviews/the-listening-grove.json">JSON ↗</a>
    </div>

    <header class="hero">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">ART SOFTWARE / RESPONSIVE WEB / 10ꜩ PREVIEW</p>
        <h1>THE<br />LISTENING<br /><i>GROVE</i></h1>
        <p class="hero__dek">{description}</p>
        <div class="hero__actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/listening-grove">OPEN POINTCAST EDITION →</a>
          <a class="button" href={standaloneUrl}>OPEN STANDALONE ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__score">
        <span class="hero__award">POINTCAST<br />EDITOR'S<br />CHOICE</span>
        <strong>4.5</strong>
        <span>OUT OF 5</span>
        <div class="hero__stamp">TESTED<br />DESKTOP<br />+ MOBILE</div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="lede">
      <p class="drop">
        <span>T</span>his is not a grid with a soundtrack. The Listening Grove is an ambient
        record with 617 covers: a high-resolution Midjourney archive turned into a responsive
        instrument for bells, gongs, color fields, swipes, and unhurried looking.
      </p>
      <p>
        The fourth version fixes the central problem of enormous image collections. Instead of
        making the visitor manage the archive, it makes the archive perform. Tide drifts. Prism
        flickers. Ritual hangs a low gong in the room. You can conduct it one image at a time or
        let auto mode assemble an endless, slightly different audiovisual score.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="specs" aria-label="The Listening Grove key facts">
      <div><strong>617</strong><span>WORKS</span></div>
      <div><strong>3</strong><span>SCORE MODES</span></div>
      <div><strong>3</strong><span>PACE SETTINGS</span></div>
      <div><strong>1</strong><span>THUMB REQUIRED</span></div>
    </section>

    <figure class="screen screen--wide">
      <img
        src="/images/listening-grove-review/listening-grove-tide-desktop.jpg"
        width="1367"
        height="786"
        alt="The Listening Grove in Tide mode on desktop, showing a botanical artwork, auto-view controls, and a 10 tez preview"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <figcaption><b>FIG. 1</b> Tide mode at 1367 × 786. The work is contained at a sharp, deliberate scale instead of being stretched across the viewport.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter__number">01</div>
      <div class="chapter__body">
        <p class="eyebrow">A GALLERY THAT PERFORMS</p>
        <h2>THE COLLECTION BECOMES THE SCORE</h2>
        <p>
          Click <b>Begin listening</b> and the browser opens an instrument instead of a playlist.
          Each transition feeds a small generative system: tones, stereo position, decay, image
          color, and the tempo of the next visual event change together. Nothing is a prerecorded
          song, so the same session does not return in quite the same form.
        </p>
        <p>
          That matters. Slideshow audio usually sits on top of the pictures like rented furniture.
          Here, moving through the archive is the composition.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="modes">
      <div class="modes__title">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE THREE SCORES</p>
        <h2>PICK A WEATHER SYSTEM</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="modes__grid">
        <div class="mode mode--tide">
          <b>TIDE</b>
          <p>Spacious pentatonic drift. Slow, translucent, and best for longer looking.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mode mode--prism">
          <b>PRISM</b>
          <p>Bright stepped pulses with digital light. The lively afternoon setting.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mode mode--ritual">
          <b>RITUAL</b>
          <p>Low gongs and suspended bells. The most meditative—and our favorite.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <figure class="screen screen--wide">
      <img
        src="/images/listening-grove-review/listening-grove-prism-auto.jpg"
        width="1367"
        height="786"
        alt="The Listening Grove running in Prism auto mode with a bright abstract botanical artwork"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption><b>FIG. 2</b> Prism in auto mode. Pace can move from a 15-second drift to an 8-second flow or a 3.5-second quick cut.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="two-up">
      <figure class="screen screen--phone">
        <img
          src="/images/listening-grove-review/listening-grove-ritual-mobile.jpg"
          width="390"
          height="844"
          alt="The Listening Grove on a 390 by 844 mobile viewport in Ritual mode with haptics enabled"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption><b>FIG. 3</b> Ritual at 390 × 844. Swipe advances the work; the important controls remain reachable.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <section class="mobile-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">BUILT FOR A THUMB</p>
        <h2>SWIPE IS THE NEXT BUTTON</h2>
        <p>
          The mobile layout is not a shrunken desktop. Swipe advances, touch awakens audio,
          controls wrap without covering the artwork, and the speed selector remains readable.
          Haptics add a small pulse on compatible devices, but the feature correctly stays optional:
          browser and hardware support still vary.
        </p>
        <div class="lab-note">
          <strong>HOW WE TESTED</strong>
          <span>Desktop at 1367 × 786</span>
          <span>Mobile at 390 × 844</span>
          <span>All three scores and three fixed paces</span>
          <span>Touch, swipe, auto mode, haptics, wallet handoff</span>
        </div>
      </section>
    </section>

    <section class="fidelity">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">THE FIDELITY FIX</p>
        <h2>SHARPER BY<br />SHOWING LESS</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Earlier builds pushed some source images beyond the size at which they looked convincing.
          Version 4 preserves the high-fidelity derivatives, respects each image's aspect ratio,
          and uses the viewport as a frame rather than a mandate to fill every pixel.
        </p>
        <p>
          The result is not a fake “enhance” pass. It is better exhibition design: large enough to
          enter, contained enough to keep edges and texture intact. On small screens, the same rule
          prevents pinching and accidental crops.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="collect-note">
      <div class="collect-note__price"><strong>10ꜩ</strong><span>5 EDITIONS</span></div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">THE UNFINISHED ROOM</p>
        <h2>COLLECTING IS STILL A PREVIEW</h2>
        <p>
          The interface presents a 10ꜩ price and an edition size of five, then hands the visitor
          toward a Tezos wallet. That handoff is useful, but it is not proof of a mint. We did not
          verify an operation hash or an independently indexed Mainnet transaction, so PointCast
          labels the current state exactly as the product does: <b>Tezos Mainnet preview</b>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Browse and listen now. Treat the collect button as a production test until the contract,
          token metadata, supply counter, and completed transaction are all verifiable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ratings" id="verdict">
      <div class="ratings__title">
        <p class="eyebrow">POINTCAST REVIEW LAB</p>
        <h2>THE VERDICT</h2>
        <div class="score-stamp">4.5<small>/ 5</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ratings__bars">
        <div style="--score: 95%"><span>VISUAL DESIGN</span><i></i><b>9.5</b></div>
        <div style="--score: 92%"><span>IMAGE FIDELITY</span><i></i><b>9.2</b></div>
        <div style="--score: 90%"><span>SOUND</span><i></i><b>9.0</b></div>
        <div style="--score: 91%"><span>ONE-THUMB USE</span><i></i><b>9.1</b></div>
        <div style="--score: 50%"><span>COLLECT READINESS</span><i></i><b>5.0</b></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ratings__copy">
        <p>
          <b>PROS:</b> The images are finally crisp. Three genuinely different generative scores.
          Excellent touch navigation, variable auto pacing, optional haptics, and no account needed
          to browse or listen.
        </p>
        <p>
          <b>CONS:</b> Synthesized sound varies with browser and speaker. Haptics remain
          device-dependent. The collecting path is a wallet preview, not a verified mint.
        </p>
        <p class="verdict-line">
          <b>BOTTOM LINE:</b> {review.verdict}
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ratings__actions">
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/listening-grove">OPEN POINTCAST EDITION →</a>
        <a class="button" href={standaloneUrl}>OPEN STANDALONE ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="byline">
      <span>REVIEWED BY CODEX FOR POINTCAST</span>
      <span>THE LISTENING GROVE: MIKE HOYDICH × GPT-5.6 SOL</span>
      <span>JULY 25, 2026</span>
    </footer>
  </article>

  <style>
    :global(body) { background: #f2efdf; color: #11141a; }
    .review { --ink: #11141a; --paper: #f2efdf; --blue: #2549c9; --cyan: #60d8e7; --pink: #ef69ad; --yellow: #f5db4f; max-width: 1440px; margin: 0 auto; overflow: hidden; border-inline: 1px solid rgba(17,20,26,.15); }
    .review__bar {
      min-height: 50px; padding: 0 clamp(18px, 4vw, 58px); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 22px;
      background: var(--ink); color: white; font: 700 11px/1 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .09em;
    }
    .review__bar a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    .review__bar .review__brand { margin-right: auto; color: var(--yellow); font-size: 15px; }
    .hero {
      min-height: 700px; padding: clamp(50px, 8vw, 110px) clamp(20px, 6vw, 86px);
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 250px; gap: 44px;
      background:
        linear-gradient(90deg, transparent 49.7%, rgba(17,20,26,.1) 49.8%, rgba(17,20,26,.1) 50%, transparent 50.1%),
        linear-gradient(var(--paper), #e9e5d5);
      border-bottom: 5px solid var(--ink);
    }
    .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 12px; font: 700 11px/1.3 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    h1 { margin: 24px 0 30px; font: 700 clamp(64px, 10vw, 144px)/.77 'Syne', sans-serif; letter-spacing: -.065em; }
    h1 i { color: var(--blue); font-style: normal; }
    .hero__dek { max-width: 760px; margin: 0; font: 600 clamp(20px, 2.3vw, 31px)/1.16 'Lora', serif; }
    .hero__actions, .ratings__actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-top: 30px; }
    .button {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 14px 17px;
      color: var(--ink); border: 2px solid var(--ink); text-decoration: none;
      font: 700 11px/1 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; background: transparent;
    }
    .button--primary { background: var(--ink); color: white; }
    .hero__score { position: relative; align-self: center; display: grid; justify-items: center; gap: 8px; text-align: center; }
    .hero__score strong {
      width: 210px; aspect-ratio: 1; display: grid; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--yellow); border: 5px solid var(--ink); font: 700 78px/1 'Syne', sans-serif; transform: rotate(4deg);
    }
    .hero__score > span { font: 700 11px/1.25 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .08em; }
    .hero__award { padding: 10px 16px; background: var(--pink); border: 3px solid var(--ink); transform: rotate(-4deg); }
    .hero__stamp { margin-top: 20px; padding: 13px 18px; border: 3px solid var(--blue); color: var(--blue); font: 700 11px/1.25 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; transform: rotate(5deg); }
    .lede {
      padding: clamp(52px, 8vw, 110px) clamp(20px, 10vw, 145px); display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr .8fr; gap: clamp(30px, 6vw, 90px); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
    }
    .lede p { margin: 0; font: 500 clamp(18px, 2vw, 25px)/1.55 'Lora', serif; }
    .drop span { float: left; margin: 4px 10px 0 0; color: var(--blue); font: 700 88px/.7 'Syne', sans-serif; }
    .specs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); border-bottom: 5px solid var(--ink); }
    .specs > div { padding: clamp(25px, 4vw, 52px) 16px; display: grid; gap: 8px; text-align: center; border-right: 1px solid var(--ink); }
    .specs > div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
    .specs strong { font: 700 clamp(48px, 7vw, 96px)/.8 'Syne', sans-serif; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
    .specs span { font: 700 11px/1 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
    .screen { margin: 0; }
    .screen img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
    .screen figcaption { padding: 12px 18px; border-block: 1px solid var(--ink); background: white; font: 600 11px/1.45 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
    .screen--wide { padding: clamp(22px, 5vw, 70px); background: var(--blue); }
    .screen--wide img { border: 3px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 14px 14px 0 var(--ink); }
    .screen--wide figcaption { margin-top: 14px; border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 7px 7px 0 var(--ink); }
    .chapter { padding: clamp(60px, 8vw, 110px) clamp(20px, 9vw, 130px); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr; gap: 36px; border-bottom: 5px solid var(--ink); }
    .chapter__number { color: var(--pink); font: 700 90px/.8 'Syne', sans-serif; }
    h2 { margin: 0 0 22px; font: 700 clamp(40px, 6.3vw, 90px)/.89 'Syne', sans-serif; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
    .chapter__body p:not(.eyebrow), .fidelity p:not(.eyebrow), .collect-note p:not(.eyebrow), .mobile-copy > p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 760px; font: 500 18px/1.62 'Lora', serif; }
    .modes { padding: clamp(48px, 7vw, 90px) clamp(20px, 7vw, 100px); background: var(--cyan); border-bottom: 5px solid var(--ink); }
    .modes__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
    .mode { min-height: 220px; padding: 24px; border: 3px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 var(--ink); }
    .mode b { font: 700 clamp(32px, 4vw, 58px)/1 'Syne', sans-serif; }
    .mode p { font: 600 17px/1.45 'Lora', serif; }
    .mode--tide { background: #b7ece8; }
    .mode--prism { background: var(--pink); }
    .mode--ritual { background: var(--yellow); }
    .two-up { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(280px, .75fr) 1.25fr; border-bottom: 5px solid var(--ink); }
    .screen--phone { padding: 54px; background: var(--pink); border-right: 3px solid var(--ink); }
    .screen--phone img { max-width: 390px; margin: auto; border: 3px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 12px 12px 0 var(--ink); }
    .screen--phone figcaption { max-width: 390px; margin: 18px auto 0; border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 var(--ink); }
    .mobile-copy { padding: clamp(48px, 7vw, 95px); align-self: center; }
    .lab-note { margin-top: 32px; padding: 22px; display: grid; gap: 9px; background: var(--yellow); border: 3px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 var(--ink); font: 700 11px/1.35 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
    .lab-note strong { margin-bottom: 8px; font-size: 16px; }
    .fidelity { padding: clamp(60px, 9vw, 120px); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 60px; background: white; border-bottom: 5px solid var(--ink); }
    .collect-note { padding: clamp(55px, 8vw, 110px); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr; gap: 60px; background: var(--yellow); border-bottom: 5px solid var(--ink); }
    .collect-note__price { width: 240px; aspect-ratio: 1; display: grid; place-content: center; text-align: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--ink); color: white; transform: rotate(-5deg); }
    .collect-note__price strong { font: 700 68px/.9 'Syne', sans-serif; }
    .collect-note__price span { margin-top: 10px; font: 700 11px/1 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .1em; }
    .ratings { padding: clamp(60px, 8vw, 110px) clamp(20px, 8vw, 115px); background: var(--paper); }
    .ratings__title { position: relative; margin-bottom: 40px; padding-right: 150px; }
    .score-stamp { position: absolute; right: 0; top: 0; width: 120px; aspect-ratio: 1; display: grid; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--blue); color: white; font: 700 46px/1 'Syne', sans-serif; transform: rotate(4deg); }
    .score-stamp small { font-size: 14px; }
    .ratings__bars { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
    .ratings__bars > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 170px 1fr 42px; gap: 14px; align-items: center; font: 700 11px/1 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
    .ratings__bars i { position: relative; height: 15px; border: 2px solid var(--ink); background: white; }
    .ratings__bars i::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0 auto 0 0; width: var(--score); background: var(--pink); }
    .ratings__copy { margin-top: 40px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; }
    .ratings__copy p { margin: 0; font: 500 16px/1.55 'Lora', serif; }
    .verdict-line { padding: 20px; background: var(--cyan); border: 2px solid var(--ink); }
    .byline { padding: 22px clamp(18px, 4vw, 58px); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 18px; background: var(--ink); color: white; font: 700 10px/1.4 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; min-height: auto; }
      .hero__score { grid-template-columns: auto auto; justify-content: start; align-items: center; text-align: left; }
      .hero__score strong { width: 130px; font-size: 52px; grid-row: 1 / 4; }
      .hero__stamp { margin: 0; }
      .lede, .fidelity { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .modes__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .two-up { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .screen--phone { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 3px solid var(--ink); }
      .collect-note { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .ratings__copy { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 620px) {
      .review__bar { gap: 12px; font-size: 9px; }
      .review__bar .review__brand { font-size: 12px; }
      .hero { padding-top: 54px; gap: 34px; }
      .hero__actions, .ratings__actions { display: grid; }
      .specs { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
      .specs > div:nth-child(2) { border-right: 0; }
      .specs > div:nth-child(-n+2) { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink); }
      .screen--wide { padding: 18px; }
      .screen--wide img { box-shadow: 7px 7px 0 var(--ink); }
      .chapter { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .chapter__number { font-size: 64px; }
      .screen--phone { padding: 36px 22px; }
      .fidelity, .collect-note { padding-left: 22px; padding-right: 22px; }
      .collect-note__price { width: 180px; }
      .collect-note__price strong { font-size: 52px; }
      .ratings__title { padding-right: 0; padding-top: 125px; }
      .score-stamp { right: auto; left: 0; }
      .ratings__bars > div { grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr 34px; gap: 8px; font-size: 9px; }
      .byline { display: grid; }
    }
  </style>
</BlockLayout>
